CommitDate: Sat Sep 19 09:17:14 2026 -0500

    fix(api): honor env/lang filters on GET /api/v1/problems when q is empty (OB-GAP-080)
    
    The non-search branch of handleListProblems passed only status to
    ListProblemClassesWithCountsFiltered/CountProblemClasses, silently
    ignoring the documented env= and lang= exact-match filters. The q
    branch (Search/SearchCount) already honored them, so ?env=<nonsense>
    returned the full catalog without q but total=0 with q — and the SPA
    hits exactly that shape when a filter chip is clicked with an empty
    query box.
    
    Both store methods now take env, lang and apply the same EXISTS
    exact-match semantics as Search (empty = no filter; a class matches
    when one of its answer rows carries the value; filters intersect and
    compose with status). All callers updated. RED-proven: reverting
    store.go/handlers.go makes TestListProblems_EnvLangFiltersWithoutQuery
    fail with total=2 for env=<nonsense> (the bug verbatim).
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
